{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1085512-yantras-yet-again","id":1085512,"title":"Yantras yet again","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-04-29T11:20:54-07:00","id":1085512,"title":"Yantras yet again","content":"I was rereading the legacy section in the main book, and noticed that it states that anyone can be initiated into a legacy, independent of path or order, if one has developed a praxis that duplicates the legacy's initial attainment, and uses one of the legacy's yantras. So how would one learn the yantra? The only way I can find for a mage to learn a yantra other than the standardized magical tools, environments, or high speech/sigils is to learn them from a legacy. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","name":"Newes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-29T13:10:57-07:00","id":1085549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1085512-yantras-yet-again#post1085512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was rereading the legacy section in the main book, and noticed that it states that anyone can be initiated into a legacy, independent of path or order, if one has developed a praxis that duplicates the legacy's initial attainment, and uses one of the legacy's yantras. So how would one learn the yantra? The only way I can find for a mage to learn a yantra other than the standardized magical tools, environments, or high speech/sigils is to learn them from a legacy.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could model it off of getting a new dedicated tool, you have to keep using it in a Yantra slot and getting +0 dice for a while before it becomes an effective Yantra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-29T18:12:59-07:00","id":1085636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1085512-yantras-yet-again#post1085512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So how would one learn the yantra? The only way I can find for a mage to learn a yantra other than the standardized magical tools, environments, or high speech/sigils is to learn them from a legacy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sacraments and dedicated tools are the big ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-30T05:10:05-07:00","id":1085756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1085512-yantras-yet-again?p=1085549#post1085549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You could model it off of getting a new dedicated tool, you have to keep using it in a Yantra slot and getting +0 dice for a while before it becomes an effective Yantra.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. Assuming there are not actually any current rules about how to get a new Yantra outside of joining a legacy (and there don't seem to be - maybe in SoS, may it come soon. SOON!), this is a good house rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","name":"Newes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-30T05:23:18-07:00","id":1085759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1085512-yantras-yet-again?p=1085636#post1085636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sacraments and dedicated tools are the big ones.</div> </div> </div> </div> I don't see how this would work. You only have one dedicated magical tool, which I assume mages choose VERY early on in their magely career (before anything that would link to a legacy starts to be an issue), and they don't see to be the same type of yantras used by legacies. <br /> <br /> Also, I didn't think sacramental yantras worked that way, in as much as I thought every sacramental yantra was a one time thing, not a specific tool (even using tool in this case to refer to a process or action).<br /> <br /> The closest thing I can think of in examples of exiting legacies to something that could start as a sacramental legacy is the use of stimulants by the 11th question, but even that is not how I thought sacramental yantras worked. I would think drinking coffee could only count as a sacramental yantra MAYBE if it was part of a spell (probably life) to stay alert / focused (whereas the legacy in question uses the action of the stimulants themselves to create alertness as a yantra to other effects, if I understand the write up).<br /> <br /> If you were just suggesting these as examples of how to house rule, and not suggesting these are meant in RAW as ways to develop legacy specific yantras, then just ignore the above.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","name":"Newes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-30T07:20:23-07:00","id":1085775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1085512-yantras-yet-again?p=1085759#post1085759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I didn't think sacramental yantras worked that way, in as much as I thought every sacramental yantra was a one time thing, not a specific tool (even using tool in this case to refer to a process or action).</div> </div> </div> </div>Habitually baking herbs and spices into bread to infuse it with healing magic is logically going to help you align your soul with a Legacy that heals people with bread that has a special blend of herbs and spices in it.<br /> <br /> Legacies Yantras are where a good chunk of the flavor behind their Theory and aesthetics comes into prominence; the adherents of a forgotten god in the Temenos are going to benefit from idols and symbols and the symbolic panoply of the entity in question, and a conspiracy of rogue photographers is going to have more members pulled from outside the parent Path/Order who use photographs as sacraments than sculptures or sketches.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-30T07:56:14-07:00","id":1085784,"title":"","content":"It makes perfect sense to me. Want to join the Eleventh Question as a Mysteriym Mastigos, learn Perfect Timing as a Praxis and drink some coffee as a Sacrament every time you use it. I don't see the disconnect. Alternatively, if the Legacy you want to join doesn't have any Yantras that work as sacriments, you could always break your Dedicated Tool and spend a month using one of the legacy's more physical Yantras as a +0 Tool on all of your spells until it becomes Dedicated for you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T02:07:45-07:00","id":1087579,"title":"","content":"I'm of the mind that all you really need to use a tool is have it make sense with your magical style, and that implies having a rational that makes it fall in line. That would seem to be why it could help you attain the Legacy; If you have that rational and have substantiated it into your magical style, then you are coming into alignment with how the Legacy does things (probably).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1547-bunnirabbi","name":"BunniRabbi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1547_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}